<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Botha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis Botha was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> general and statesman. He helped found the Nieuwe Republiek in 1884, rose to command the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> forces in the Second Boer War and afterwards worked for reconciliation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Prime Minister of the self-governing Transvaal Colony from 1907, he became the first Prime Minister of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1910 and led it into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-south-west-africa">German South West Africa</a> in 1915.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-botha.jpg" alt="Louis Botha" width="154" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louisbotha_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Men formed in the republic’s service, among them <b>Louis Botha</b> and Jan Smuts, went on to lead the Union of South Africa.</blockquote><a href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>By the Treaty of Vereeniging in 1902 the two Boer republics became British colonies, and in 1906–1907 they received responsible government, which brought the Afrikaner generals <b>Louis Botha</b> and Jan Smuts to power in the Transvaal.</blockquote><a href="/empire/union-of-south-africa">Union of South Africa · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1884 Boers led by Lucas Meyer, among them the young <b>Louis Botha</b>, backed Dinuzulu, son of Cetshwayo, against Zibhebhu, and in return claimed a huge tract of Zulu land, where they proclaimed the Nieuwe Republiek with Lucas Meyer as president.</blockquote><a href="/state/nieuwe-republiek">Nieuwe Republiek</a></li><li><blockquote>Self-government came in 1907, and the Het Volk party of <b>Louis Botha</b> and Jan Smuts won the election.</blockquote><a href="/state/transvaal-colony">Transvaal Colony</a></li></ul></section>
